+# [P0] Enforce authentication on Studio /admin routes (AdminShell mounts for logged-out visitors)
+
+## Task ID
+`bridge-20261027-studio-admin-guard`
+
+## Target repository
+`Supremeai-bd/supremeai-studio` (tracked on the public `supremeai-open` task board per federation policy).
+
+## Severity
+**P0 — unauthenticated visitors can mount the full admin console UI.** Backend authorization is NOT claimed compromised; the defect is client-side route guarding that fails closed only by accident of backend 401s, while exposing the entire admin surface, module names, and internal UI structure to anonymous visitors.
+
+## Verified evidence (pulled live via MCP tower, 2026-10-26)
+- `github_read_file {repo:"supremeai-studio", path:"src/App.tsx"}` (12,506 chars): both `/admin` and `/admin/*` routes are wrapped ONLY in `<RoleGuard requiredRole="admin">` (+ ErrorBoundary) — **no `ProtectedRoute` wrapper**:
+  ```tsx
+  <Route path="/admin" element={<RoleGuard requiredRole="admin"><ErrorBoundary><AdminShell /></ErrorBoundary></RoleGuard>} />
+  <Route path="/admin/*" element={<RoleGuard requiredRole="admin"><ErrorBoundary><AdminShell /></ErrorBoundary></RoleGuard>} />
+  ```
+- `github_read_file {repo:"supremeai-studio", path:"src/components/core/guards/RoleGuard.tsx"}` (sha `c9b2e0658457`, 4,668 chars) contains:
+  ```tsx
+  if (isChecking) return <AuthLoadingSpinner />;
+  if (!isAuthenticated) return <>{children}</>; // ProtectedRoute already handles unauthenticated redirect
+  ```
+- The comment's assumption ("ProtectedRoute already handles unauthenticated redirect") is false on these routes — nothing else guards `/admin`, so `children` (the full `AdminShell`) renders for unauthenticated visitors.
+
+## Why this blocks production
+- Information disclosure: module inventory, route structure, internal labels, and UI flows of the admin console are visible pre-auth.
+- Defense-in-depth violation: the UI should never render an admin shell for an anonymous identity even if every backend call 401s.
+- If any admin child page renders meaningful content before its first API call (or caches state in localStorage), the exposure grows beyond structure.
+
+## Remediation plan (smallest safe change)
+1. Wrap both `/admin` routes with the existing `ProtectedRoute` component (outside `RoleGuard`), OR invert `RoleGuard`'s unauthenticated branch to render the redirect/denied state by default with an explicit opt-in for the deferred pattern.
+2. Add a route-guard test: unauthenticated visit to `/admin` and `/admin/*` must redirect to login (assert AdminShell never mounts).
+3. Sweep other privileged routes (`/jarvis`, OperatorCockpit paths) for the same pattern in the same change or an immediate follow-up.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- [ ] `/admin` + `/admin/*` unauthenticated → redirect to login; `AdminShell` never mounted
+- [ ] Regression test green in CI
+- [ ] Audit of other guarded routes documented
+
+## Related orders
+- Audit "SupremeAI সমন্বিত Executive Diagnosis" (2026-10-26), P0 item 6 (admin access-control defect).
